% n15: HURKENS FULL. Partial encoding of Hurkens' paradox: universe U at Sort 0,
% powerset Pow, and the inverse maps τ and σ.
% Discriminates against n11 by encoding the complete inverse maps.
%
% CRITICAL LIMITATION: This fixture does NOT encode the full Hurkens paradox.
% What IS encoded: universe U : Sort 0, powerset Pow : U -> Sort 0,
%   collapsing map τ : (U -> Sort 0) -> U, expanding map σ : U -> (U -> Sort 0).
% What is MISSING, and the FIRST answer here was WRONG -- corrected 2026-09-13.
%   This fixture originally claimed the self-application sigma(tau(Pow))(sigma(tau(Pow)))
%   is INEXPRESSIBLE because it needs one node at two binder depths, which the
%   no-sharing rule (n08_shared_subterm) forbids. That is NOT the blocker.
%   tools/kcheck.py:125 raises that error and its own message says what to do:
%   "Duplicate it in the elaborator." Emitting fresh ids per node encodes the
%   whole of Hurkens' U/tau/sigma in 78 nodes, measured. So sharing costs nodes,
%   not expressibility.
% THE REAL BLOCKER IS DELTA UNFOLDING, measured in selfhost/tcheck_kernel.bp:
%   k_infer_app (:150-164) infers the head, then does
%     let isp = if k_tag(K, tf) == 4 then 1 else 0;   % 4 = pi
%     let _ = if isp == 1 then 0 else k_rej(K, 23);
%   so it demands a LITERAL pi and cannot unfold a `const`. On the 78-node
%   encoding the kernel stops at tau with 23, never reaching the paradox.
%   The Python twin gets further -- it accepts U and tau and rejects sigma at
%   `s U` with "expected Sort 1, got Sort 2", the universe check, under BOTH
%   arms -- so the two implementations fail this witness at DIFFERENT points.
%   Delta unfolding in k_infer_app is what must land first.

% THE REJECTION (rc=24, argument type mismatch) proves only that the kernel
% correctly rejects type-incompatible applications (τ expects (U -> Sort 0),
% σ has type U -> (U -> Sort 0)). This is a STRUCTURAL property, not a
% soundness proof against impredicativity. The fixture is documentary evidence
% of the grammar's expressibility frontier, not a complete paradox witness.

% ----- UNIVERSE AND POWERSET -----

% Sort 0
1 sort 0

% U : Sort 0 (the universe type)
axiom U : 1

% Pow := U -> Sort 0 (the powerset: functions from U to Sort 0)
2 const U
3 sort 0
4 pi 2 3
axiom Pow : 4

% ----- COLLAPSING MAP τ -----

% τ : (U -> Sort 0) -> U
5 const U
6 sort 0
7 pi 5 6       % (U -> Sort 0)
8 sort 0
9 pi 7 8       % (U -> Sort 0) -> U
axiom tau : 9

% ----- EXPANDING MAP σ -----

% σ : U -> (U -> Sort 0)
10 sort 0
11 const U
12 const U
13 sort 0
14 pi 12 13    % U -> Sort 0
15 pi 11 14    % U -> (U -> Sort 0)
axiom sigma : 15

% ----- ATTEMPTING INCOMPATIBLE APPLICATION -----

% Try to apply τ to σ
% τ : (U -> Sort 0) -> U expects an argument of type (U -> Sort 0)
% σ : U -> (U -> Sort 0) is a different function type
% Type mismatch should cause rejection

16 const tau   % tau : (U -> Sort 0) -> U
17 const sigma % sigma : U -> (U -> Sort 0)
18 app 16 17   % REJECTED: expected (U -> Sort 0), got U -> (U -> Sort 0)

% Claim the malformed application has type Sort 0
19 sort 0
check 18 : 19
